  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CMAC Cusco: Equity Investment to Support the Growth of MSEs in Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BID Invest states its intention to become a shareholder in Caja Municipal de Ahorro y Cr&#xe9;dito Cusco (the &#x201c;Caja&#x201d; or &#x201c;Caja Cusco&#x201d;), for an amount equivalent in Peruvian soles (&#x201c;PEN&#x201d;) of up to ~US$20.6 million (the &#x201c;Investment&#x201d; or the &#x201c;Project&#x201d;).The Investment is expected to represent a minimum of 7.5% of the Caja&#x2019;s total shares. The objective of the Investment is to strengthen the Caja&#x2019;s capital structure (&#x201c;Tier I&#x201d;), which benefits the capital adequacy ratio and supports the continued sustainable growth of the Micro and Small Enterprises (&#x201c;MSEs&#x201d;) in Peru.</narrative>
  </description>
